      "body": "[Godbolt](https://godbolt.org/z/3ba8Ers5q) indicates 152 -> 144 bytes on 64-bit (with no change on 32-bit, as mentioned in the PR description).\r\nI wouldn't claim a total RAM saving though, as it seems allocator-dependent: glibc gives the map nodes 200 bytes in both cases.\r\nBut I don't see a downside to the swap, since the fields initialize independently and serialization is unchanged.\r\n\r\nACK d9387c41c1c2076ce035aeb6a3daf7bfd83f7c32",
